      "content": "To temporarily protect the wound, it's important to first clean it with gentle soap and warm water. Then, apply gentle pressure to stop the bleeding if necessary. Use an antibacterial ointment to keep it moist, which can help prevent infection. You can cover the wound with a clean, dry bandage or gauze. However, please understand that while these steps can offer temporary protection, they are not a substitute for proper medical treatment. A tetanus shot update may also be warranted depending on when your last booster was. If attending a clinic or calling your doctor is absolutely not possible, make sure the wound is located in a clean environment, and the temporary dressing is changed regularly. It is still critical to visit a healthcare professional as soon as your schedule allows to assess the wound and provide necessary care. Even a small wound can become serious if not properly tended to.",
